      "kind": "narrative",
      "text": "I’d start with the Turkish Airlines business-class award leaving San Francisco at 2:05 p.m.: among the shown choices it arrives at the same time as the earlier business option, with a shorter reported elapsed journey. The tradeoff is that it requires a separate San Francisco–Los Angeles ticket, and award seats and taxes are unverified. These are selected search results, not the full inventory; the search provider reported partial coverage, so confirm current availability and prices before booking.",
      "label": null,
      "reference_kind": null,
      "canonical_id": null,
      "journey": null,
      "component": null,
      "lead": null,
      "unavailable": false
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "text": "January 8 departure from SFO at 2:05 p.m.; arrive in Bangkok January 10 at 8:50 a.m. The award portion is Turkish Airlines business class, reported as 275,000 Turkish miles, routing LAX–IST–BKK with a 60-minute connection in Istanbul. The San Francisco–Los Angeles positioning flight is a separate American ticket, quoted at USD 139.00 with unknown price scope. The 164-minute wait at LAX is a separate-booking connection, not evidence of ticket protection. Turkish does not provide reliable seat-count or tax-and-fee evidence here; support for the requested one traveler is unknown, and the award tax quote is unavailable. The reported award cabin does not establish each leg’s cabin.",
